# Dev Tools
#
# List of dev tools I prefer. The list is ordered: highest preference comes
# first, within each Category. The configuration in this repo mostly revolves
# around these tools, and a few more. This file is under development, so more
# tools will be added.
#
# Only current tools and AI tools go here. Tools I tried, used before, or want
# to try go in work dev_tools_archive.md:
# https://github.com/raveensrk/work/blob/main/deck/tools/dev_tools_archive.md
# A tool lives in one file only.
#
# Level is how hard a tool is to learn well, not how much I prefer it:
#   1 Beginner      useful within minutes
#   2 Easy          the basics take a few hours
#   3 Intermediate  takes days; has its own concepts or config to learn
#   4 Advanced      takes weeks; needs a deep mental model
#   5 Expert        takes months or years to master
#
# Tier is how much a tool matters to me, not how hard it is: base is the
# core kit, extra adds what I use often, max is everything. Views build on
# each other (extra shows base too), so a tool never requires one of a higher
# tier.
#
# The learning path is the Edge records: From must be known before To. Every
# edge into a tool is required (AND); edges that share an Any value are
# either-one (OR). A prerequisite never has a higher Level or Tier than the
# tool it unlocks, there are no loops, and a prerequisite already implied
# through another one is not repeated. The %graph lines say so, and
# draw_graph enforces them.
#
# Edit:   draw_graph dev_tools.rec   (a graph editor: https://github.com/raveensrk/draw_graph)
# Check:  draw_graph check dev_tools.rec
# Query:  recsel -t Node -e 'Level = 1' -p Name dev_tools.rec
#         recsel -t Edge -e 'To = "Rust"' -p From dev_tools.rec
# Pos is where draw_graph shows a tool, `x y` in px; layout only. Group puts
# a tool in a named box (Group: Browser).

%rec: Group
%key: Name
%type: Parent rec Group
%type: Collapsed enum yes no
%allowed: Name Label Parent Color Collapsed Note
%graph: parent Parent

Name: LLM data

Name: Browser

Name: VPN

%rec: Node
%key: Name
%type: Level range 1 5
%type: Tier enum base extra max
%type: Group rec Group
%type: Pos regexp /^-?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+$/
%mandatory: Name Category Level Tier
%allowed: Name Category Subcategory Level Tier Url Note Group Pos
%graph: label Name
%graph: color Level
%graph: filter Tier
%graph: group Group
%graph: pos Pos

